# Komunyon

Bible studies and communion groups in The Hague only. Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, and the Firebase JS SDK. Data access is client-side.

## Stack

- Strict TypeScript. Routes and layouts live in `src/app`.
- One `'use client'` `AuthProvider` owns Firebase Auth state.
- Import the modular SDK only: `firebase/app`, `firebase/auth`, `firebase/firestore`, `firebase/storage`.
- Do not add the Firebase Admin SDK, Next.js route handlers, or server actions for study or profile data.

## Firestore

- `users/{uid}` — a user may write only their own profile, and may delete that profile. A finished profile needs a picture, name, age, country, city, phone number, and a Hague neighbourhood when the city is The Hague. Bio is optional. Deleting the account also deletes every study they host and removes them from studies they joined. An open study then says it is no longer listed.
- `studies/{studyId}` — a direct link can be read without an account, so the shared page can show the study card. The city list still includes a study only when `isPublic` is true or the field is missing. `isPublic: false` is listed only for a signed-in `hostId`, uids in `invitedUserIds`, and uids in `approvedUserIds`. Host snapshot, neighbourhood, schedule, capacity, tags (`bible-study`, `prayer`, `worship`, `communion`), `pendingUserIds`, `approvedUserIds`, `invitedUserIds`. A recurring study may list `skippedDates` as `YYYY-MM-DD` sessions that will not meet. The street address is never on this document.
- `studies/{studyId}/private/details` — `exactAddress` and `entryNotes` only. Readable by `hostId` and uids in `approvedUserIds`. Writable by the host. An approved member also sees the host phone from `users/{hostId}`; that number is never copied onto the study.
- `studies/{studyId}/notices/{uid}` — a member may write only their own notice: “left” while approved, “cancelled” while pending, or “accepted” / “declined” while invited. The host may write a “removed” notice for someone still approved, and may read and delete notices. The member may read and delete their own notice.
- `studies/{studyId}/sessions/{yyyy-mm-dd}` — the session id is that date. The host and approved members can read the description. Only the host can write it. The description is at most 4000 characters.
- Never write `exactAddress` or `entryNotes` onto `studies/{studyId}`.
- Only `hostId` may edit or delete a study, approve or decline requests, or remove an approved member.
- Anyone else may only add or remove their own uid in `pendingUserIds`, remove their own uid from `approvedUserIds`, or accept or decline their own uid on `invitedUserIds`. Accepting an invite also adds that uid to `approvedUserIds`.

```ts
import { doc, updateDoc, arrayUnion } from 'firebase/firestore';

await updateDoc(doc(db, 'studies', studyId), {
  pendingUserIds: arrayUnion(uid),
});
```

A profile photo is the Google account photo URL, or a JPEG stored in Cloud Storage at `avatars/{uid}`. Session files live at `sessions/{studyId}/{yyyy-mm-dd}/{uid}-{time}.jpg`, `.txt`, or an audio extension (`webm`, `m4a`, `mp3`, `ogg`, `wav`). The host and approved members can read them. Only the host can add or remove them. Older profile pictures may still be a small JPEG on the user document.
